WEBVTT

00:00:06.199 --> 00:00:10.163
Take your brother outside as
fast as you can! Now Dean! Go!

00:00:12.005 --> 00:00:13.808
Mary! No!

00:00:16.332 --> 00:00:18.114
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.052
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:21.165 --> 00:00:22.487
Jess excuse us.

00:00:25.048 --> 00:00:26.441
I swore I was done hunting,

00:00:27.074 --> 00:00:27.791
For good.

00:00:27.863 --> 00:00:28.734
I can't do this alone.

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:31.915
Now you're taking off the middle of the
night to spend the week-End with them.

00:00:31.916 --> 00:00:34.416
Hey, everything's gonna be OK.

00:00:34.459 --> 00:00:35.729
I promise.

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:39.018
You think mom would
have wanted this for us?

00:00:39.151 --> 00:00:40.966
Dean, we were raised like warriors.

00:00:41.021 --> 00:00:44.105
You have a responsability.
To dad and his cruisade.

00:00:44.238 --> 00:00:47.650
Even if you do find the thing
that killed her, mom's gone

00:00:48.046 --> 00:00:50.216
And she isn't coming back.

00:00:50.753 --> 00:00:52.882
Don't talk about her like that.

00:00:54.028 --> 00:00:54.985
Dad's gone.

00:00:55.046 --> 00:00:56.689
I've got his journal.
He left me a message.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:59.004
It's coordinates he
left us. It's weird, man.

00:00:59.087 --> 00:00:59.681
Hey, Dean,

00:00:59.791 --> 00:01:00.745
What I said earlier,

00:01:00.823 --> 00:01:02.169
I'm sorry.

00:01:02.748 --> 00:01:04.172
No chick-Flick moments.

00:01:05.944 --> 00:01:06.977
Yes.

00:01:16.335 --> 00:01:17.399
No!

00:01:28.478 --> 00:01:31.012
We got work to do.

00:02:09.459 --> 00:02:10.879
Dude, you're cheating.

00:02:11.206 --> 00:02:13.376
No, you just suck.

00:02:19.641 --> 00:02:22.683
Hey, Hailey. Day six. We're
still out near Black Water Ridge.

00:02:22.684 --> 00:02:26.684
We're fine, keeping safe, so
don't worry. Talk to you tomorrow.

00:02:36.011 --> 00:02:38.400
Hey, where you going?
My moment of victory.

00:02:38.522 --> 00:02:40.065
Nature calls.

00:03:22.289 --> 00:03:23.272
Brad?

00:03:24.951 --> 00:03:26.566
Gary, what's going on?

00:04:44.485 --> 00:04:47.146
I am, um...

00:04:47.848 --> 00:04:53.280
You always said roses were
lame, so, I brought you, uh...

00:05:08.147 --> 00:05:09.566
Jess...

00:05:10.626 --> 00:05:11.908
Oh, god.

00:05:16.609 --> 00:05:18.274
I should have protected you.

00:05:18.784 --> 00:05:21.322
I should have told you the truth.

00:05:37.974 --> 00:05:39.353
You okay?

00:05:39.762 --> 00:05:41.086
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:05:41.973 --> 00:05:43.365
Another nightmare?

00:05:49.233 --> 00:05:50.994
Want to drive for a while?

00:05:53.496 --> 00:05:56.690
In your whole life, you
never once asked me that.

00:05:57.148 --> 00:05:59.583
Just thought you might
want to. Never mind.

00:06:00.309 --> 00:06:01.404
Look, man,

00:06:01.957 --> 00:06:04.288
You're worried about
me. I get it, and ...

00:06:04.476 --> 00:06:08.184
Thank you, but I'm perfectly okay.

00:06:11.256 --> 00:06:13.665
All right. Where are we?

00:06:14.072 --> 00:06:16.747
We are just outside of Grand Junction.

00:06:20.916 --> 00:06:24.264
You know what? Maybe we shouldn't
have left Stanford so soon.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:28.332
Sam, we dug around there for a
week. We came up with nothing.

00:06:28.696 --> 00:06:32.451
If you want to find the thing that
killed Jessica... Got to find dad first.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:37.505
Dad disappearing, and this thing
showing up again after 20 years?

00:06:37.744 --> 00:06:39.590
It's no coincidence.

00:06:40.028 --> 00:06:43.407
Dad will have answers. He'll
know what to do. It's weird, man.

00:06:43.767 --> 00:06:47.193
These coordinates he left
us, this Black Water Ridge...

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:49.800
What about it? There's nothing there.

00:06:50.394 --> 00:06:52.871
It's just woods.

00:06:54.607 --> 00:06:57.408
Why is he sending us to
the middle of nowhere?

00:07:04.355 --> 00:07:06.655
So Black Water Ridge is pretty remote.

00:07:06.764 --> 00:07:10.131
It's cut off by these canyons
here --Rough terrain, dense forest,

00:07:10.132 --> 00:07:12.632
Abandoned silver and gold
mines all over the place...

00:07:12.757 --> 00:07:16.047
Dude, check out the size
of this friggin' bear.

00:07:18.582 --> 00:07:22.227
And a dozen or more
grizzlies in the area.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:25.017
It's no nature hike, that's for sure.

00:07:25.408 --> 00:07:29.147
You boys aren't planning to go out
near Black Water Ridge, by any chance?

00:07:29.413 --> 00:07:34.534
Oh, no, sir. We're environmental-Study majors
from U.C. Boulder-Just working on a paper.

00:07:34.628 --> 00:07:36.176
Recycle, man.

00:07:36.479 --> 00:07:37.621
Bull.

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:41.204
You're friends with
that Hailey girl, right?

00:07:42.523 --> 00:07:43.149
Yes.

00:07:43.587 --> 00:07:45.151
Yes, we are.

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:47.702
Ranger... Wilkinson.

00:07:48.535 --> 00:07:50.755
Well, I will tell you
exactly what I told her.

00:07:50.756 --> 00:07:56.156
Her brother filled out a backcountry permit saying
he wouldn't be back from Black Water until the 24th.

00:07:56.258 --> 00:07:58.808
So it's not exactly a
missing persons now, is it?

00:07:59.418 --> 00:08:02.500
Tell that girl to quit worrying.
I'm sure her brother's just fine.

00:08:02.657 --> 00:08:03.987
We will.

00:08:04.769 --> 00:08:06.819
Well, that Hailey girl's
quite a pistol, huh?

00:08:06.948 --> 00:08:08.654
That is putting it mildly.

00:08:08.815 --> 00:08:13.219
Actually, you know what would help is if I
could show her a copy of that backcountry permit.

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:16.920
You know, so she could see
her brother's return date.

00:08:18.223 --> 00:08:20.695
Yeah. Heh heh.

00:08:20.836 --> 00:08:22.635
What, are you cruising
for a hookup or something?

00:08:22.697 --> 00:08:23.448
What do you mean?

00:08:23.562 --> 00:08:26.101
The coordinates point to Black Water
Ridge. So what are we waiting for?

00:08:26.102 --> 00:08:29.602
Let's just go find dad.
Why even talk to this girl?

00:08:29.711 --> 00:08:33.919
I don't know, maybe we should know what we're
walking into before we actually walk into it.

00:08:34.841 --> 00:08:35.780
What?

00:08:35.858 --> 00:08:39.160
Since when are you all "shoot
first, ask questions later" anyway?

00:08:39.426 --> 00:08:40.849
Since now.

00:08:42.774 --> 00:08:44.307
Oh, really?

00:08:47.813 --> 00:08:49.409
You must be Hailey Collins.

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:53.552
I'm Dean, this is Sam. We're rangers with the
park service. Ranger Wilkinson sent us over.

00:08:53.553 --> 00:08:57.253
We wanted to ask you some
questions about your brother Tommy.

00:08:58.191 --> 00:09:00.006
Let me see some I.D.

00:09:02.909 --> 00:09:04.161
There you go.

00:09:10.951 --> 00:09:13.689
Come on in. Thanks.

00:09:14.894 --> 00:09:15.754
That yours?

00:09:15.989 --> 00:09:16.568
Yeah.

00:09:16.709 --> 00:09:17.820
Nice car.

00:09:22.741 --> 00:09:26.574
So, if Tommy's not due back for a
while, how do you know something's wrong?

00:09:26.813 --> 00:09:31.041
He checks in every day by cell. He
e-Mails photos, stupid little videos.

00:09:31.042 --> 00:09:33.542
But we haven't heard anything
in over three days now.

00:09:33.803 --> 00:09:35.743
Well, maybe he can't get cell reception.

00:09:36.045 --> 00:09:37.735
He's got a satellite phone, too.

00:09:38.126 --> 00:09:42.788
Could it be he's just having fun and
forgot to check in? He wouldn't do that.

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:47.194
Our parents are gone. It's
just my two brothers and me.

00:09:47.195 --> 00:09:49.695
We all keep pretty
close tabs on each other.

00:09:50.273 --> 00:09:53.120
Can I see the pictures
he sent you? Yeah.

00:09:54.012 --> 00:09:55.436
That's Tommy.

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:04.794
Hey, Hailey. Day six. We're
still out near Black Water Ridge.

00:10:04.795 --> 00:10:08.795
We're fine, keeping safe, so don't
worry, okay? Talk to you tomorrow.

00:10:10.472 --> 00:10:13.714
We'll find your brother. We're heading
out to Black Water Ridge first thing.

00:10:13.715 --> 00:10:16.215
Then maybe I'll see you there.

00:10:17.168 --> 00:10:18.029
Look.

00:10:18.221 --> 00:10:20.067
I can't sit around here anymore,

00:10:20.302 --> 00:10:24.166
So I hired a guide. I'm heading out in the
morning, and I'm gonna find Tommy myself.

00:10:24.922 --> 00:10:27.201
I think I know how you feel.

00:10:29.334 --> 00:10:31.650
Hey, you mind forwarding these to me?

00:10:31.916 --> 00:10:32.886
Sure.

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:41.159
So, Black Water Ridge doesn't get a
lot of traffic-Local campers mostly--

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:46.160
But, still, this past april, two hikers went
missing out there. They were never found.

00:10:46.227 --> 00:10:47.541
Any before that?

00:10:47.619 --> 00:10:48.230
Yeah.

00:10:48.277 --> 00:10:51.317
In 1982, eight different people
all vanished in the same year.

00:10:51.318 --> 00:10:53.518
Authorities said it
was a grizzly attack.

00:10:53.518 --> 00:10:58.718
And, again, in 1959, and
again, before that, in 1936.

00:10:58.827 --> 00:11:02.094
Every 23 years, just like clockwork.

00:11:02.535 --> 00:11:04.054
Okay, watch this.

00:11:04.283 --> 00:11:05.900
Here's the clincher.

00:11:06.788 --> 00:11:11.688
I downloaded that guy Tommy's
video to the laptop. Check this out.

00:11:13.028 --> 00:11:14.514
Do it again.

00:11:17.608 --> 00:11:22.949
That's three frames. It's a fraction of a
second. Whatever that thing is, it can move.

00:11:23.913 --> 00:11:26.249
I told you something weird was going on.

00:11:26.576 --> 00:11:29.222
Yeah. I got one more thing.

00:11:29.348 --> 00:11:34.280
In '59, one camper survived the
supposed grizzly attack, just a kid

00:11:34.477 --> 00:11:36.567
Barely crawled out of the woods alive.

00:11:36.907 --> 00:11:38.315
Is there a name?

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:42.934
Look, ranger, I don't know why
you're asking me about this.

00:11:43.076 --> 00:11:45.923
It's public record. I was a kid.

00:11:46.126 --> 00:11:48.473
My parents got mauled by a... grizzly?

00:11:48.668 --> 00:11:50.154
That's what attacked them?

00:11:58.465 --> 00:12:00.702
The other people that
went missing that year,

00:12:00.906 --> 00:12:02.940
Those bear attacks, too?

00:12:05.178 --> 00:12:07.682
What about all the people
that went missing this year?

00:12:08.401 --> 00:12:09.997
Same thing?

00:12:12.098 --> 00:12:16.240
If we knew what we were dealing
with, we might be able to stop it.

00:12:18.169 --> 00:12:20.797
I seriously doubt that.

00:12:21.204 --> 00:12:22.283
Anyways,

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:25.939
I don't see the
difference it would make.

00:12:27.222 --> 00:12:29.099
You wouldn't believe me.

00:12:29.428 --> 00:12:31.649
Nobody ever did.

00:12:34.385 --> 00:12:35.872
Mr. Shaw

00:12:38.938 --> 00:12:40.815
What did you see?

00:12:45.396 --> 00:12:46.835
Nothing.

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:51.654
It moved too fast to see.

00:12:51.701 --> 00:12:53.312
It hid too well.

00:12:53.426 --> 00:12:54.913
I heard it, though.

00:12:55.507 --> 00:12:57.478
A roar

00:12:59.231 --> 00:13:00.123
Like ...

00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:03.776
No man or animal I ever heard.

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:05.869
It came at night?

00:13:06.558 --> 00:13:08.435
Got inside your tent?

00:13:08.753 --> 00:13:11.241
It got inside our cabin.

00:13:12.039 --> 00:13:15.919
I was sleeping in front of
the fireplace when it came in.

00:13:16.565 --> 00:13:19.647
It didn't smash a
window or break the door,

00:13:20.293 --> 00:13:22.312
It unlocked it.

00:13:23.094 --> 00:13:26.943
Do you know of a bear that
could do something like that?

00:13:27.605 --> 00:13:31.438
I didn't even wake up until
I heard my parents screaming.

00:13:31.673 --> 00:13:32.815
It killed them?

00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:35.224
Dragged them off into the night.

00:13:37.758 --> 00:13:43.093
Why it left me alive --I've been
asking myself that ever since.

00:13:47.525 --> 00:13:49.700
It did leave me this, though.

00:13:59.657 --> 00:14:03.521
There's something evil in those woods.

00:14:06.259 --> 00:14:08.653
It was some sort of a demon.

00:14:09.127 --> 00:14:12.651
Spirits and demons don't have to unlock
doors. They just go through the walls.

00:14:12.652 --> 00:14:15.652
So it's probably something
else -Something corporeal.

00:14:15.781 --> 00:14:16.876
"Corporeal"?

00:14:17.142 --> 00:14:18.394
Excuse me, professor.

00:14:18.539 --> 00:14:20.401
Shut up. So, what do you think?

00:14:20.917 --> 00:14:23.358
The claws, the speed that it moves.

00:14:23.686 --> 00:14:25.830
It could be a skinwalker,
maybe a black dog

00:14:25.984 --> 00:14:30.615
Whatever we're talking about, we're talking
about a creature, and it's corporeal,

00:14:30.756 --> 00:14:32.873
Which means we can kill it.

00:14:50.020 --> 00:14:52.273
We cannot let that
Hailey girl go out there.

00:14:52.335 --> 00:14:56.093
Oh yeah, what are we gonna tell her she can't go
into the woods because of a big, scary monster?

00:14:56.094 --> 00:14:58.094
Yeah.

00:14:58.833 --> 00:15:00.179
Her brother's missing, Sam.

00:15:00.382 --> 00:15:02.087
She's not just gonna sit this out.

00:15:02.385 --> 00:15:06.583
No, we go with her, we protect her, and we keep
our eyes peeled for our fuzzy predator friend

00:15:06.677 --> 00:15:08.601
So finding dad's not enough?

00:15:10.999 --> 00:15:13.205
Now we got to babysit, too?

00:15:15.990 --> 00:15:16.976
What?

00:15:18.274 --> 00:15:19.307
Nothing.

00:15:26.341 --> 00:15:29.443
I'll tell you again. I
don't think ben should come.

00:15:30.054 --> 00:15:31.258
Roy...

00:15:31.733 --> 00:15:36.489
Look, you're paying me good money to keep
everybody safe. I think Ben's safest at home.

00:15:46.753 --> 00:15:48.395
You guys got room for two more?

00:15:48.588 --> 00:15:50.262
You want to come with us?

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:51.248
Who are these guys?

00:15:51.295 --> 00:15:54.659
Apparently, this is all the
park service could muster up.

00:15:54.710 --> 00:15:56.025
You're rangers?

00:15:56.072 --> 00:15:56.916
That's right.

00:15:57.073 --> 00:16:00.124
And you're hiking out
in biker boots and jeans?

00:16:01.391 --> 00:16:04.051
Well, sweet heart, I don't do shorts.

00:16:06.017 --> 00:16:10.413
Oh, you think this is funny? It's dangerous
backcountry out there. Her brother might be hurt.

00:16:12.791 --> 00:16:15.341
Believe me, I know how
dangerous it can be.

00:16:15.902 --> 00:16:18.374
We just want to help them
find their brother. That's all.

00:17:16.804 --> 00:17:19.135
Roy, you said you did a little hunting.

00:17:19.406 --> 00:17:21.393
Yeah, more than a little.

00:17:23.302 --> 00:17:25.011
What kind of furry critters do you hunt?

00:17:25.168 --> 00:17:27.655
Mostly buck. Sometimes bear.

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:32.693
Tell me, uh, Bambi or
Yogi ever hunt you back?

00:17:36.706 --> 00:17:38.928
What you doing, Roy?

00:17:44.924 --> 00:17:47.553
You should watch where
you're stepping... ranger.

00:17:51.449 --> 00:17:53.561
It's a bear trap.

00:17:59.673 --> 00:18:01.957
You didn't pack any provisions.

00:18:02.066 --> 00:18:03.896
You guys are carrying a duffel bag.

00:18:04.006 --> 00:18:07.072
You're not rangers, so
who the hell are you?

00:18:15.642 --> 00:18:17.566
Sam and I are brothers,

00:18:17.864 --> 00:18:19.491
And we're looking for our father.

00:18:19.670 --> 00:18:21.126
He might be here. We don't know.

00:18:21.266 --> 00:18:24.239
I just figured that you and
me, we're in the same boat.

00:18:25.887 --> 00:18:29.532
Why didn't you just tell me that
from the start? I'm telling you now.

00:18:30.017 --> 00:18:33.100
Besides, it's probably the most
honest I've ever been with a woman...

00:18:33.647 --> 00:18:34.914
Ever.

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:37.641
So, we okay?

00:18:41.631 --> 00:18:43.446
Yeah, okay.

00:18:43.967 --> 00:18:46.298
And what do you mean I
didn't pack provisions?

00:19:03.077 --> 00:19:04.532
This is it.

00:19:04.939 --> 00:19:06.143
Black Water Ridge.

00:19:06.206 --> 00:19:08.068
What coordinates are we at?

00:19:12.026 --> 00:19:14.237
35 and minus 111.

00:19:19.572 --> 00:19:20.573
You hear that?

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:21.793
Yeah.

00:19:23.399 --> 00:19:25.151
Not even crickets.

00:19:25.918 --> 00:19:27.811
I'm gonna go take a look around.

00:19:28.176 --> 00:19:30.444
You shouldn't go off by yourself.

00:19:30.554 --> 00:19:33.996
That's sweet. Don't worry about me.

00:19:42.086 --> 00:19:45.951
All right, everybody
stays together. Let's go.

00:19:54.629 --> 00:19:56.663
Hailey! Over here!

00:20:04.257 --> 00:20:05.587
Oh, my god.

00:20:05.978 --> 00:20:07.746
Looks like a grizzly.

00:20:24.357 --> 00:20:25.530
Tommy?

00:20:27.329 --> 00:20:28.424
Tommy!

00:20:28.894 --> 00:20:31.401
Tommy! Shh... Shh...

00:20:32.195 --> 00:20:33.149
Why?

00:20:33.587 --> 00:20:35.214
Something might still be out there.

00:20:36.095 --> 00:20:37.128
Sam.

00:20:44.689 --> 00:20:47.181
The bodies were dragged
from the campsite.

00:20:48.292 --> 00:20:51.390
But here, the tracks just vanish.

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:53.408
It's weird.

00:20:55.567 --> 00:20:57.820
I tell you what.

00:20:58.290 --> 00:21:00.840
It's no skinwalker or black dog.

00:21:23.853 --> 00:21:26.231
Hey, he could still be alive.

00:21:30.126 --> 00:21:32.270
Help!

00:21:53.747 --> 00:21:56.579
It seemed like it was coming
from around here, didn't it?

00:22:02.556 --> 00:22:04.746
Everybody back to camp.

00:22:10.761 --> 00:22:12.325
Our packs!

00:22:12.967 --> 00:22:16.002
So much for my GPS
and my satellite phone.

00:22:16.116 --> 00:22:17.477
What the hell's going on?

00:22:17.571 --> 00:22:18.682
It's smart.

00:22:18.760 --> 00:22:21.200
It wants to cut us off
so we can't call for help.

00:22:21.419 --> 00:22:25.534
You mean someone --Some nut job
out there just stole all our gear.

00:22:25.617 --> 00:22:28.980
I need to speak with you... in private.

00:22:37.850 --> 00:22:40.401
Okay, let me see dad's journal.

00:22:46.228 --> 00:22:47.104
All right.

00:22:47.980 --> 00:22:49.044
Check that out.

00:22:50.171 --> 00:22:51.438
Oh, come on.

00:22:51.709 --> 00:22:55.613
Windigos are in the Minnesota woods or Northern
Michigan. I've never even heard of one this far west.

00:22:55.514 --> 00:23:01.614
Think about it, Dean -The claws,
the way it can mimic a human voice.

00:23:01.974 --> 00:23:02.960
Great.

00:23:03.617 --> 00:23:05.620
Well, then this is useless.

00:23:10.313 --> 00:23:12.519
We got to get these people to safety.

00:23:14.595 --> 00:23:17.380
All right, listen up. It's time to go.

00:23:17.662 --> 00:23:21.213
Things have gotten more complicated.

00:23:21.844 --> 00:23:22.235
What?

00:23:22.329 --> 00:23:24.848
Whatever's out there,
I think I can handle it.

00:23:24.910 --> 00:23:29.463
If you shoot this thing, you're just
gonna make it mad. We have to leave now.

00:23:29.494 --> 00:23:32.476
One, you're talking nonsense, two, you're
in no position to give anybody orders.

00:23:32.477 --> 00:23:33.677
Relax.

00:23:33.832 --> 00:23:36.398
We never should have let you come
out in the first place, all right?

00:23:36.477 --> 00:23:37.478
I'm trying to protect you.

00:23:37.556 --> 00:23:38.651
You protect me?

00:23:38.797 --> 00:23:41.001
I was hunting these woods when your
mommy was still kissing you good night.

00:23:41.002 --> 00:23:41.802
Yeah.

00:23:41.895 --> 00:23:44.648
It's a
damn-Near-Perfect hunter.

00:23:45.149 --> 00:23:46.870
It's smarter than you.

00:23:47.344 --> 00:23:52.742
And it's gonna hunt you down and eat you alive
unless we get your stupid sorry ass out of here.

00:23:52.773 --> 00:23:54.729
You know you're crazy, right? Yeah?

00:23:54.901 --> 00:23:57.518
You ever hunt -Chill out.

00:23:57.581 --> 00:24:01.758
Stop! Stop it. Everybody just stop.

00:24:02.545 --> 00:24:03.390
Look.

00:24:03.640 --> 00:24:06.097
Tommy might still be alive.

00:24:06.597 --> 00:24:09.163
And I'm not leaving here without him.

00:24:13.629 --> 00:24:15.741
It's getting late.

00:24:16.852 --> 00:24:19.277
This thing is a good hunter in the day,

00:24:19.887 --> 00:24:22.250
But an unbelievable hunter at night.

00:24:22.724 --> 00:24:25.008
We'll never beat it
--Not in the dark.

00:24:27.057 --> 00:24:29.404
We need to settle
inand protect ourselves.

00:24:30.390 --> 00:24:32.158
How?

00:24:41.657 --> 00:24:44.880
One more time.That's...?
Anasazi symbols.

00:24:45.036 --> 00:24:48.775
It's for protection. The
windigo can't cross over them.

00:24:49.703 --> 00:24:52.190
Nobody likes a skeptic, Roy.

00:25:02.604 --> 00:25:05.733
You want to tell me what's going
on in that freaky head of yours?

00:25:07.465 --> 00:25:09.546
Dean... No, you're not fine.

00:25:10.234 --> 00:25:12.753
You're like a powder keg,
man. It's not like you.

00:25:13.426 --> 00:25:16.117
I'm supposed to be the
belligerent one, remember?

00:25:20.131 --> 00:25:21.868
Dad's not here.

00:25:24.262 --> 00:25:29.805
I mean, that much we know for sure, right? He
would have left us a message, a sign, right?

00:25:30.697 --> 00:25:32.512
Yeah, you're probably right.

00:25:33.815 --> 00:25:36.631
To tell you the truth, I don't
think dad's ever been to Lost Creek.

00:25:38.461 --> 00:25:41.747
Then let's get these people back
to town, and let's hit the road...

00:25:42.018 --> 00:25:45.757
Go find dad. I mean, why
are we still even here?

00:25:54.425 --> 00:25:55.926
This is why...

00:25:56.349 --> 00:25:58.211
This book.

00:25:58.649 --> 00:26:03.942
This is dad's single most valuable possession.
Everything he knows about every evil thing is in here.

00:26:04.036 --> 00:26:06.320
And he's passed it on to us.

00:26:07.123 --> 00:26:09.939
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:26:10.925 --> 00:26:13.788
You know, saving
people, hunting things...

00:26:14.054 --> 00:26:16.307
The family business.

00:26:18.867 --> 00:26:20.322
That makes no sense.

00:26:20.479 --> 00:26:27.660
Why-Why doesn't he just call us? Why doesn't
he tell us what he wants, tell us where he is?

00:26:28.944 --> 00:26:30.571
I don't know.

00:26:32.261 --> 00:26:33.810
But the way I see it,

00:26:35.171 --> 00:26:38.394
Dad's given us a job to
do, and I intend to do it.

00:26:38.754 --> 00:26:40.084
Dean...

00:26:40.819 --> 00:26:41.711
No.

00:26:42.853 --> 00:26:44.464
I gotta find dad.

00:26:45.278 --> 00:26:47.281
I gotta find Jessica's killer.

00:26:53.203 --> 00:26:58.460
It's the only thing I can think about. Okay.
All right. Sam, we'll find them. I promise.

00:26:59.790 --> 00:27:00.968
Listen to me.

00:27:01.140 --> 00:27:03.268
You've got to prepare yourself.

00:27:04.175 --> 00:27:06.366
I mean, this search could take a while.

00:27:07.122 --> 00:27:08.828
And all that anger,

00:27:09.031 --> 00:27:12.614
You can't keep it burning over
the long haul. It's gonna kill you.

00:27:13.620 --> 00:27:15.560
You got to have patience, man.

00:27:18.098 --> 00:27:19.709
How do you do it?

00:27:20.507 --> 00:27:22.744
How does dad do it?

00:27:24.137 --> 00:27:26.452
Well, for one, them.

00:27:27.161 --> 00:27:31.385
I mean, I figure our family's so screwed
to hell, maybe we can help some others.

00:27:31.687 --> 00:27:33.971
It makes things a
little bit more bearable.

00:27:39.081 --> 00:27:41.131
And I'll tell you what else helps...

00:27:43.462 --> 00:27:47.405
Killing as many evil sons
of bitches as I possibly can.

00:27:50.046 --> 00:27:51.642
Help me!

00:27:54.833 --> 00:27:56.147
Please...!

00:28:00.458 --> 00:28:01.788
Help!

00:28:03.133 --> 00:28:04.651
It's trying to draw us out.

00:28:04.929 --> 00:28:06.385
Just stay cool. Stay put.

00:28:06.517 --> 00:28:08.556
Inside the magic circle?

00:28:08.645 --> 00:28:10.381
Help!

00:28:11.872 --> 00:28:13.437
Help me!

00:28:15.862 --> 00:28:17.864
Okay, that's no grizzly.

00:28:23.332 --> 00:28:26.429
It's okay. We'll be
all right. I promise.

00:28:29.938 --> 00:28:31.863
It's here.

00:28:38.392 --> 00:28:39.565
I hit it!

00:28:39.612 --> 00:28:40.645
Roy, no!

00:28:41.176 --> 00:28:42.303
Roy!

00:28:42.913 --> 00:28:44.274
Don't move.

00:28:48.534 --> 00:28:51.412
It's over here. Ugh!

00:28:53.045 --> 00:28:54.077
Roy?!

00:29:20.822 --> 00:29:21.871
I don't...

00:29:22.340 --> 00:29:25.328
I mean, these types of things--
They aren't supposed to be real.

00:29:25.563 --> 00:29:27.268
I wish I could tell you different.

00:29:28.478 --> 00:29:30.527
How do we know it's not
out there watching us?

00:29:31.059 --> 00:29:32.217
We don't.

00:29:33.250 --> 00:29:34.819
But we're safe for now.

00:29:36.243 --> 00:29:38.089
How do you know about this stuff?

00:29:40.655 --> 00:29:42.439
It kind of runs in the family.

00:29:48.121 --> 00:29:49.138
Hey.

00:29:50.233 --> 00:29:53.269
So, we've got half a
chance in the daylight.

00:29:53.570 --> 00:29:55.870
And I, for one...

00:29:56.355 --> 00:29:58.843
Want to kill this evil son of a bitch.

00:29:59.724 --> 00:30:01.601
Well, hell, you know I'm in.

00:30:02.013 --> 00:30:04.934
Windigo is a cree indian word.
It means, "evil that devours."

00:30:04.935 --> 00:30:06.535
They're hundreds of years old.

00:30:06.597 --> 00:30:12.875
Each one was once a man, sometimes an indian or
other times a frontiers manor a miner or hunter.

00:30:13.021 --> 00:30:16.181
How's a man turn into one of those
things? Well, it's always the same.

00:30:16.291 --> 00:30:17.699
During some harsh winter,

00:30:17.840 --> 00:30:21.235
A guy finds himself starving,
cut off from supplies or help

00:30:21.475 --> 00:30:26.043
Becomes a cannibal to survive, eating
other members of his tribe or camp.

00:30:26.121 --> 00:30:28.030
Like the donner party.

00:30:28.774 --> 00:30:32.548
Cultures all over the world believe that eating
human flesh gives a person certain abilities--

00:30:32.549 --> 00:30:35.549
Speed, strength, immortality.

00:30:35.633 --> 00:30:37.147
If you eat enough of it,

00:30:37.350 --> 00:30:39.635
Over years, you become this ...

00:30:39.838 --> 00:30:42.216
Less-Than-Human
thing.

00:30:42.379 --> 00:30:44.256
You're always hungry.

00:30:44.350 --> 00:30:48.199
So, if that's true, how
can Tommy still be alive?

00:30:50.374 --> 00:30:52.491
You're not gonna like it. Tell me.

00:30:52.819 --> 00:30:56.214
More than anything, a windigo knows
how to last long winters without food.

00:30:56.297 --> 00:30:59.332
It hibernates for years
at a time. When it's awake,

00:30:59.739 --> 00:31:02.904
It keeps its victims
alive. It stores them

00:31:03.233 --> 00:31:05.579
So it can feed whenever it wants.

00:31:06.706 --> 00:31:11.905
If your brother's alive, it's keeping
him somewhere dark, hidden, and safe

00:31:12.562 --> 00:31:14.408
And we got to track it back there.

00:31:14.549 --> 00:31:16.463
And then how do we stop it?

00:31:16.572 --> 00:31:17.652
Well,

00:31:17.918 --> 00:31:20.984
Guns are useless-So are knives.

00:31:22.006 --> 00:31:23.664
Basically...

00:31:24.071 --> 00:31:26.950
We gotta torch the sucker.

00:31:43.214 --> 00:31:44.231
Dean.

00:31:47.423 --> 00:31:48.549
What is it?

00:32:06.598 --> 00:32:07.865
You know,

00:32:08.210 --> 00:32:12.403
I was thinking that those claw
prints, so clear and distinct

00:32:14.050 --> 00:32:16.428
They were almost too easy to follow.

00:32:42.512 --> 00:32:46.250
You okay? His neck's broken.

00:32:46.986 --> 00:32:49.776
Run, run! Go, go, go, go, go!

00:32:58.946 --> 00:33:02.106
Come on. I got you. I got you.

00:33:11.990 --> 00:33:13.352
Hailey!

00:33:23.364 --> 00:33:24.678
Dean!

00:33:26.185 --> 00:33:29.767
If it keeps its victims
alive, why would it kill Roy?

00:33:29.971 --> 00:33:31.003
Honestly?

00:33:31.379 --> 00:33:34.524
I think because Roy shot
at it, he pissed it off.

00:33:42.133 --> 00:33:43.698
They went this way.

00:33:49.602 --> 00:33:51.745
It's better than bread crumbs.

00:35:33.924 --> 00:35:37.898
Hey, it's okay. It's okay. It's okay.

00:35:50.251 --> 00:35:51.409
Dean.

00:35:53.724 --> 00:35:55.195
You. Wake up.

00:35:56.060 --> 00:35:58.547
Dean. Hey. You okay?

00:36:01.113 --> 00:36:02.208
Yeah.

00:36:02.495 --> 00:36:04.779
Hailey... Hailey.

00:36:05.076 --> 00:36:07.173
Wake up. Wake up.

00:36:08.377 --> 00:36:09.520
Gotcha.

00:36:19.692 --> 00:36:22.681
You sure you're all right?
Yeah, yeah. Where is it?

00:36:22.780 --> 00:36:24.626
It's gone for now.

00:36:45.331 --> 00:36:46.207
Tommy.

00:36:49.727 --> 00:36:50.510
Tommy.

00:36:56.684 --> 00:36:58.280
Cut him down.

00:37:11.841 --> 00:37:13.625
We're gonna get you home.

00:37:14.537 --> 00:37:15.945
Check it out.

00:37:16.763 --> 00:37:19.298
Flare guns. Those will work.

00:37:33.750 --> 00:37:37.928
Looks like someone's home for
supper. We'll never out run it.

00:37:41.980 --> 00:37:44.452
You thinking what I'm
thinking? Yeah, I think so.

00:37:47.883 --> 00:37:50.501
All right, listen to me. Stay with
Sam. He's gonna get you out of here.

00:37:50.502 --> 00:37:52.202
What are you gonna do?

00:37:54.819 --> 00:37:57.494
It's chow time, you freakin' bastard!

00:37:57.823 --> 00:38:02.078
Yeah, that's right! Bring
it on, baby! I taste good!

00:38:10.049 --> 00:38:12.255
All right, come on. Hurry!

00:38:17.522 --> 00:38:18.758
Hey!

00:38:19.979 --> 00:38:22.247
Hey, you want some white meat, bitch?!

00:38:22.435 --> 00:38:23.765
I'm right here!

00:38:39.316 --> 00:38:40.930
Get him out of here. Sam, no.

00:38:40.931 --> 00:38:42.931
Go. Go!

00:38:43.321 --> 00:38:43.962
Go.

00:38:53.378 --> 00:38:54.317
Come on.

00:38:55.708 --> 00:38:56.663
Come on.

00:39:11.821 --> 00:39:12.697
Sam!

00:39:14.689 --> 00:39:17.802
Come on. Hurry, hurry, hurry! Go!

00:39:30.584 --> 00:39:32.086
Get behind me.

00:40:15.165 --> 00:40:17.449
Not bad, huh?

00:40:25.605 --> 00:40:30.893
That's when it circled the campsite. I mean,
this grizzly must have weighed 800, 900 pounds.

00:40:32.744 --> 00:40:36.029
So, really, I don't
know how to thank you.

00:40:39.210 --> 00:40:42.809
Must you cheapen the moment? Yeah!

00:40:43.838 --> 00:40:46.905
You riding with your brother? Yeah.

00:40:48.485 --> 00:40:49.549
Let's go.

00:41:01.625 --> 00:41:03.878
I hope you find your father.

00:41:07.221 --> 00:41:08.707
Thanks, Sam.

00:41:26.409 --> 00:41:28.708
Man, I hate camping.

00:41:29.021 --> 00:41:30.257
Me too.

00:41:33.422 --> 00:41:35.644
Sam, you know we're
gonna find dad, right?

00:41:36.567 --> 00:41:38.632
Yeah, I know.

00:41:40.045 --> 00:41:42.267
But in the meantime

00:41:44.019 --> 00:41:45.787
I'm driving.

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:03.250
